{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,2]],"date-time":"2026-05-02T04:51:47Z","timestamp":1777697507214,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":37,"publisher":"International Union of Crystallography (IUCr)","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,25]],"date-time":"2024-01-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1706140800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,25]],"date-time":"2024-01-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1706140800000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000741","name":"University of Warwick","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["URSS"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["URSS"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000741","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iucr.org","wiley.com","iucrj.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Acta Crystallogr A Found Adv","Acta Crystallogr A","Acta Crystallogr A Found Crystallogr","Acta Cryst A","Acta Cryst A Found Adv","Acta Cryst Sect A","Acta Cryst Sect A Found Adv","Acta Crystallogr Sect A","Acta Crystallogr Sect A Found Adv","Acta Crystallogr Sect A Found Crystallogr"],"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,21]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,3,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>In electron diffraction, thermal atomic motion produces incoherent scattering over a relatively wide angular range, which appears as a diffuse background that is usually subtracted from measurements of Bragg spot intensities in structure solution methods. The transfer of electron flux from Bragg spots to diffuse scatter is modelled using complex scattering factors <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic> + <jats:italic>if<\/jats:italic>\u2032 in the Bloch wave methodology. In a two-beam Einstein model the imaginary `absorptive' scattering factor <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic>\u2032 can be obtained by the evaluation of an integral containing <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic> over all possible scattering angles. While more sophisticated models of diffuse scatter are widely used in the electron microscopy community, it is argued in this paper that this simple model is appropriate for current structure solution and refinement methods. The two-beam model is a straightforward numerical calculation, but even this simplistic approach can become time consuming for simulations of materials with large numbers of atoms in the unit cell and\/or many incident beam orientations. Here, a parameterized form of <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic>\u2032 is provided for 103 elements as neutral, spherical atoms that reduces calculation time considerably.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1107\/s2053273323010963","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,25]],"date-time":"2024-01-25T11:27:28Z","timestamp":1706182048000},"page":"146-150","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1107\/cm_01","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Parameterized absorptive electron scattering factors"],"prefix":"10.1107","volume":"80","author":[{"given":"M.","family":"Thomas","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6076-8378","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"A.","family":"Cleverley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1749-4134","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"R.","family":"Beanland","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"329","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,25]]},"reference":[{"key":"pl5034_bb1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"11644","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevB.42.11644","volume":"42","author":"Allen","year":"1990","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. B"},{"key"